-- title:
--   Mod-5 dissection setup: residue sections and the components $A_r$ of $(q;q)_\infty^3$
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring, $r\in\mathbb{N}$, and $\varphi\in R[[X]]$. This bundle defines the uncompressed section by $$[X^n]\operatorname{section5}(R,r,\varphi)=\begin{cases}[X^n]\varphi,&n\bmod5=r,\\0,&n\bmod5\ne r,\end{cases}$$ for every $n\in\mathbb{N}$. The predicate $\operatorname{IsRes5}(r,\varphi)$ means that $[X^n]\varphi=0$ whenever $n\bmod5\ne r$. Thus $r\ge5$ gives a zero section and forces a supported series to be zero. Over $(\mathbb{Z}/5\mathbb{Z})[[X]]$, it defines $A(r)$ as this section of $E(X)^3$, where $E$ is `qPochInfPS`. These are the components used in the mod-$5$ partition-congruence argument.
